{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For their vine is from the vine of Sodom.</b> The reason they lack understanding in this matter is that they take pride in their abundance of tranquility and direct all their thought to attaining the pleasures of the body alone, like the people of Sodom; and to attain this they rejected every kind of kindness, as the prophet testified, saying: הִנֵּה זֶה הָיָה עֲוֹן סְדֹם אֲחוֹתֵךְ גָּאוֹן שִׂבְעַת לֶחֶם וְשַׁלְוַת הַשְׁקֵט הָיָה לָהּ וְלִבְנוֹתֶיהָ וְיַד עָנִי וְאֶבְיוֹן לֹא הֶחֱזִיקָה (Ezekiel 16:49)." "<b>Their clusters are grapes of rosh.</b> And from this vine there grow among them grapes of rosh — that is, evil and harmful deeds — when they exert themselves to set their eyes and hearts upon their greed and upon the blood of the innocent to shed it." "<b>Bitter clusters are theirs.</b> And through this they acquire false and deceitful opinions, to speak of HaShem that which is misleading, and to say לֹא יִרְאֶה יָהּ (Psalms 94:7)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:16.897764760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}